nt.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhOEV8OxyumcNt937hGXXXsPX9nnQRF4HKk3pKLJjwJT9XAP5F1L2z5dVd67u-_dbK-vx1y08LlsZ76tSsEDHCUkW-KU6PLfQlVR2cAt3WbM4W5-S4uOJZHvX8z9vDf-PqgSmTW7S1ucxY/s320/Screenshot_2015-10-02_15-07-16.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Arcade Puppy</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arcade-puppy/</link><pubDate>Thu, 28 Jan 2010 14:54:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arcade-puppy/</guid><description>&lt;div style="float: right; margin-left: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/4310963557/" title="photo sharing"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2776/4310963557_d24485fceb_m.jpg" alt="" style="border: solid 2px #000000;" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 0.9em; margin-top: 0px;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/4310963557/"&gt;Arcade Puppy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Originally uploaded by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/people/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;While hunting about of instructions to install Python on Puppy Linux I came across Arcade Puppy.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Basically a version 4.2 variation with a lot of retro game system emulators installed.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Picture shows Arcade version of Puppy Linux running on a VirtualBox VM; running the game "Thrust" on the Spectrum emulator.&lt;br clear="all" /&gt;</description></item><item><title>The Secret Of Monkey Island on DosBox</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/secret-of-monkey-island-on-dosbox/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2009 13:57:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/secret-of-monkey-island-on-dosbox/</guid><description>&lt;div style="float: right; margin-left: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3678394450/" title="photo sharing"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm4.static.flickr.com/3638/3678394450_bb94f1c0f8_m.jpg" alt="" style="border: solid 2px #000000;" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 0.9em; margin-top: 0px;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3678394450/"&gt;The Secret Of Monkey Island on DosBox&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Originally uploaded by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/people/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Finally got round to installing DosBox on my Ubuntu laptop, now I need the time to play Monkey Island.&lt;br clear="all" /&gt;</description></item><item><title>VirtualC64 for Mac OS X</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/virtualc64-for-mac-os-x/</link><pubDate>Tue, 30 Dec 2008 10:02:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/virtualc64-for-mac-os-x/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 13 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 21 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Not a machine I had personally but did play on a friends one every now and again.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/HolyShmoly/~3/498106972/"&gt;VirtualC64 for Mac OS X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://ocaoimh.ie/" class="f"&gt;Holy Shmoly!&lt;/a&gt; by Donncha on 12/29/08&lt;/div&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.dirkwhoffmann.de/virtualc64/index.html"&gt;VirtualC64&lt;/a&gt; is a new Commodore 64 emulator for Mac OS X. It&amp;rsquo;s a promising project, let down by the fact that it&amp;rsquo;s still in beta but &lt;a href="http://code.google.com/p/virtualc64/updates/list"&gt;by the looks of things&lt;/a&gt; development is moving at a steady pace.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>